.TH SDL_PenDeviceType 3type "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 DATATYPES"
.SH NAME
SDL_PenDeviceType \- An enum that describes the type of a pen device.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_pen.h>
.PP
.BI "typedef enum SDL_PenDeviceType
.BI "{
.BI "    SDL_PEN_DEVICE_TYPE_INVALID = -1, /**< Not a valid pen device. */
.BI "    SDL_PEN_DEVICE_TYPE_UNKNOWN,      /**< Don't know specifics of this pen. */
.BI "    SDL_PEN_DEVICE_TYPE_DIRECT,       /**< Pen touches display. */
.BI "    SDL_PEN_DEVICE_TYPE_INDIRECT      /**< Pen touches something that isn't the display. */
.BI "} SDL_PenDeviceType;
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
A \(dqdirect\(dq device is a pen that touches a graphic display (like an Apple Pencil on an iPad\(aqs screen)\[char46] \(dqIndirect\(dq devices touch an external tablet surface that is connected to the machine but is not a display (like a lower-end Wacom tablet connected over USB)\[char46]
.PP
Apps may use this information to decide if they should draw a cursor; if the pen is touching the screen directly, a cursor doesn\(aqt make sense and can be in the way, but becomes necessary for indirect devices to know where on the display they are interacting\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This enum is available since SDL 3\[char46]4\[char46]0\[char46]

